 ## Overview
-Chunked World Management splits a voxel world into independent sub-worlds called chunks to allow localized mesh rebuilding, avoiding the cost of regenerating the entire world geometry when a single block changes [S1, unofficial]. It differs from flat mesh caching by introducing spatial locality: instead of one monolithic mesh, the world is a collection of smaller meshes, each managing its own voxel data and geometry [S1, unofficial].
+Chunked World Management splits a voxel world into independent sub-worlds called chunks to allow localized mesh rebuilding when a single block changes [S1, unofficial]. It differs from flat mesh caching by replacing a single monolithic mesh with a collection of smaller meshes, each managing its own voxel data and geometry [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** World coordinates of a block change (add/remove/modify).
+**Inputs:** World coordinates of a block change (add, remove, or modify).
 **Outputs:** Updated chunk data structures and GPU buffers for affected chunks.
 
