 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ for block updates (hash map lookup + set operation) [S1, unofficial]. Mesh generation is $O(V)$ where $V$ is the number of voxels in the chunk [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ for block updates due to hash map lookup and set operations [S1, unofficial]. Mesh generation is $O(V)$ where $V$ is the number of voxels in the chunk [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the total number of blocks, distributed across chunk structures [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** In the "Outpost" scene (4 chunks, 10k triangles), draw calls scale with quality settings: 37 draws/200k triangles on Low, 114 draws/879k on Balanced, 153 draws/1.87M on Ultra [S2].
-*   **Strengths:** Localized updates prevent full-world rebuilds; spatial locality improves cache coherence for mesh generation [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Overhead of managing multiple draw calls and chunk boundaries; potential for visible seams if not handled correctly [S1, unofficial].
